# nighttrain.vibe: the night-train wallpaper (see PLAN.md). neowall runs
# nighttrain.py as a terminal wallpaper, and nighttrain.glsl draws the view
# from what it prints.
#
# To try it (it replaces the wallpaper that's running):
#   neowall kill
#   neowall -f -v -c ~/.config/neowall/shaders/nighttrain/nighttrain.vibe
# Look for "Pass 0 (Buffer A): ch0=Self" in what it prints. Ctrl-C stops
# it, then `neowall` brings back the usual one.
#
# To keep it (as a machine's wallpaper), start neowall with it instead:
#   neowall -c ~/.config/neowall/shaders/nighttrain/nighttrain.vibe
# neowall doesn't reload a terminal wallpaper's shader: restart it after
# editing nighttrain.glsl. Send it a station from anywhere:
#   echo "BUILD PASSED|radar" > $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nighttrain/inbox
#
# The font size makes the terminal grid 160 x 45 cells of 24 x 48 px on a
# 3840 x 2160 screen, an exact fit, so a click lands on the cell it's over.
# The program needs no ssh agent (and no network): env drops the agent's
# socket before starting it.
default {
  terminal "env -u SSH_AUTH_SOCK python3 ~/.config/neowall/shaders/nighttrain/nighttrain.py"
  term_shader ~/.config/neowall/shaders/nighttrain/nighttrain.glsl
  term_font /usr/share/fonts/noto/NotoSansMono-Medium.ttf
  term_font_size 48
  term_cols 0
  term_rows 0
  vsync true
  shader_fps 30
}
